      "output": "All referenced code exists in this checkout and the ticket is well-scoped:\n\n- `src/pricing.ts` — `fetchModelMeta` with gateway provider pins, per-endpoint pricing, prompt/completion tiers, and cache rate fields (`input_cache_read`, `input_cache_write`) all present.\n- `src/headless-run.ts` — the `usage` and `run.completed` emit path, `cumulative` flag, `costUsd` field, `PROTOCOL_VERSION` (`v`) stamping all present.\n- `src/gateway-costs.ts` — existing gateway cost machinery.\n\nThe five acceptance criteria all orbit a single, coherent deliverable: compute cost in headless `eh run` from eh's own normalized usage × resolved gateway rates, emit it as `costUsd` + `costSource: \"gateway-rates\"`, preserve any harness-reported cost separately, avoid fabricating cost when rates are unavailable, handle cache rates, and bump the stream `v` if the shape changes. That's one focused PR, not multiple independent subsystems.\n\nThe one genuinely open decision (cache-rate fallback: bill as regular input vs zero) is explicitly delegated by AC-4 to the implementer as a documented judgment call — exactly the kind of thing resolved during planning by reading `src/pricing.ts`, not a blocker. Right repository, clear scope, sufficient acceptance signal.\n\nSTATUS:proceed\n",
