    "ticket.comments": "",
    "ticket.description": "## Problem\n\nHeadless `eh run` NDJSON `usage` events only carry `costUsd` when the inner harness self-reports one, and that number is the harness's own estimate from its internal pricing table. Measured on a real 4-lane run (2026-08-21): the grok harness reports no cost at all; Claude Code running `zai/glm-5.2` reported $1.61 where actual nebius gateway rates ($1.4/M in, $4.4/M out) put the run at $0.43 — 3.7x overstated. Anthropic-model runs happen to match only because Claude Code's table agrees with gateway pricing. eh already owns the authoritative rate source — `src/pricing.ts` (`fetchModelMeta`, gateway models + per-endpoint pricing incl. prompt/completion tiers) — but uses it only for interactive launch metadata and the statusline, never for headless run cost.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. `eh run` computes cost from its own cumulative normalized usage x the resolved model's gateway rates — honoring `--gateway-provider` pins (per-endpoint pricing, not model-aggregate) and tiered prompt/completion rates — and emits it on the final `cumulative: true` `usage` event and/or `run.completed` as `costUsd` with `costSource: \"gateway-rates\"`.\n2. A harness-reported cost, when present, is preserved in a separate field (e.g. `harnessCostUsd`), never silently preferred over the computed one.\n3. When rates are unavailable (ollama, unknown model), no fabricated cost is emitted and `costSource` says why.\n4. Cache read/write tokens are billed at the endpoint's published cache rates; when an endpoint publishes no cache rates, the chosen behavior (bill as regular input vs zero) is explicit and documented in the code.\n5. If the event shape changes, the NDJSON event `v` field is bumped per eh's versioned-stream convention.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n* Interactive-mode cost display changes.\n* Reconciliation against the Vercel AI Gateway billing dashboard.\n\nEvidence: run xcr.Syn0G9hNV6 (experimental-code-review skill, 2026-08-21) — opus lane $12.06 computed vs $12.08 harness-reported (agree), fable $12.45 vs $12.63 (agree), glm@nebius $0.43 vs $1.61 (harness wrong), grok $0.65 vs nothing (harness silent).",
